### Logowanie - ADMIN (zapisuje adminToken)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin-password-123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Logowanie - Jakub Sosnowski, USER (zapisuje jakubToken)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jakub.sosnowski@example.com",
  "password": "jakub-password-123"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("jakubToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### Scenariusz 1 - Jakub tworzy rezerwację (201, event reservation.created)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{jakubToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 3,
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2027-01-15T10:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2027-01-15T12:00:00Z"
}

> {%
  client.global.set("reservationId", response.body.id);
%}

### Scenariusz 2 - nieudana próba kolizji (409, bez eventu)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{jakubToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "roomId": 3,
  "participants": 10,
  "startTime": "2027-01-15T11:00:00Z",
  "endTime": "2027-01-15T13:00:00Z"
}

### Scenariusz 3 - ADMIN anuluje rezerwację Jakuba (200, event reservation.cancelled i powiadomienie)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Scenariusz 4 - ponowne anulowanie (200, idempotentne, bez eventu)
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/reservations/{{reservationId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log - ADMIN, od najnowszych (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log - tylko reservation.created (200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/audit-log?eventType=reservation.created&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Audit log - USER (403)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/admin/audit-log
Authorization: Bearer {{jakubToken}}
